Authors and copyright holders of note10lite-droidian
====================================================

This repository — the Droidian/Halium port of the Samsung Galaxy Note 10 Lite
(SM-N770F, codename r7, Exynos 9810) — is the original work of:

    Zulfikar Aji Kusworo (zakusworo) <greataji13@gmail.com>
        Port lead and sole author.
        Device adaptation (device-r7/), flashing and recovery tooling
        (scripts/, boot/), the D0 bring-up initramfs (initramfs/), and all
        port documentation and research notes (PROGRESS.md, BOOT-STATUS.md,
        docs/, workaround/).

Copyright (C) 2026 Zulfikar Aji Kusworo (zakusworo) <greataji13@gmail.com>

Licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2 only (GPL-2.0-only).
See LICENSE for the full text.


Provenance
----------

The companion kernel tree carries the same authorship: kernels built from the
r7 defconfigs identify themselves as

    4.9.191-samsung-r7-zakusworo

via CONFIG_LOCALVERSION in arch/arm64/configs/exynos9810-r7_defconfig and
arch/arm64/configs/exynos9810-r7_droidian_defconfig, so any device running this
port reports the author's name in `uname -r`.

Kernel changes authored for this port live on the `droidian-r7` branch of the
kernel tree and include the Waydroid enablement fixes (BRIDGE/VETH and
NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_CHECKSUM for waydroid-net, the fimc-is2 QUERYCAP
wrong-struct dereference that panicked the device on any V4L2 QUERYCAP, and the
Mali kbase pid-namespace bug that broke GPU context creation inside the
container), the framebuffer-console bootloop root-cause fix, and the Halium
debian/ packaging.


Third-party material
--------------------

Files under debug/ are diagnostic dumps captured from the device (kernel logs,
sec_log, reset reasons). They are vendor output retained as evidence for the
investigations written up in PROGRESS.md, not authored work, and no copyright
is claimed over their contents.

initramfs/init.c is written against the Linux kernel userspace ABI and the
Halium initramfs conventions; it is original code, licensed GPL-2.0-only to
stay compatible with the kernel lineage it boots.

Upstream projects this port builds on — Droidian, Halium, libhybris, ofono,
ofono-binder-plugin, ModemManager, Phosh, Waydroid — remain under their own
licenses and copyrights, held by their respective authors.


Reuse
-----

You are welcome to build on this work; that is what the GPL is for. If you do,
GPL-2.0-only requires you to keep the copyright notices above intact, state the
changes you made, and license your derivative work under the same terms. Please
also keep a visible credit to the original port and a link to
https://github.com/9810-linux/note10lite-droidian.
